# Pocket Ledger Server — Usage UI

When editing `C:\Balgram\PocketLedger-Server\sub-server\pb_public` Usage page (`#view-usage`):

- **Top row** (`.page-head-nav`): **Back** then **40px** then **Usage** title (left). **Settings gear** then **Refresh** on the **right** (gear `margin-inline-start: auto`). Intro stays below.
- Auto-refresh **30s** while the Usage page is visible (request chart **and** network meter); **stop** when the tab/window is hidden or minimized; **resume** (fresh 30s timer + one load of both charts) when it becomes visible again.
- **Top-right Refresh** reloads **both** the request chart and the network meter. Each chart still has its **own** refresh (left of Earlier) for that chart only. Refresh (click or 30s) must **not jump the page** — keep the painted UI, lock container height, restore scroll (`window.PLRefresh`).
- Chart time axis: **wheel zoom** (cursor as pivot) and **pixel-smooth drag pan**. While dragging, **load the timeline that is on screen** (debounced live fetch) so left/right bars appear without waiting for mouseup. Zoom out max **10 years**; zoom in stops at **1 minute**. Footer **Y M D H Min** matches bars: **Y** = one bar per year, **M** = one bar per month (Baisakh / January from date settings), **D** = per day, **H** = hour, **Min** = minute. Each scale click jumps the window and reloads. Each chart has its own **refresh** (left of Earlier). Click a bar drills year → month → day → hour → minute. Footer **bar / line** mode: stacked pillars vs a rising/falling total line (same hover/zoom).
- Bars sit on the **same global time axis as the timeline** (not equal index slots). Empty minutes/hours stay empty space; Y-scale does not collapse/jump when the window has gaps. Same for request chart and network meter.
- **Network meter** card sits **directly under** the Usage request chart (`#net-meter-panel`, `pb_public/network-meter.js`). Same chart chrome (Y M D H, bar/line, zoom, drag pan). Legend is Download / Upload; Y-axis is bytes. Count **this Pocket Ledger Server’s HTTP only** (API + files + panel) — never whole-PC NIC (`netstat`). Download = response bytes to clients; Upload = request bytes to the server. Do not fold it into the request-count chart. Hover popup shows **where** bytes came from (app data sync, files, live sync, this Usage panel) plus request-log actions for that minute.
- **Toolbar controls same height** (`--us-h: 32px`): Day/Hour/Minute, date range box, All users / companies / collections.
- Date = one rounded rectangle range field with an **X to clear**. Empty / today range shows **Today**. User / company / collection dropdowns also have **X** (clears back to All). Dropdown closed width 1.75in; open list grows with name, max 6in.
- Search = one field only (type in that box, no inner extra box). Click/focus keeps the existing blue ring on that same box.
- Calendar popover is a **grid, no scroll**: 3×2 / 2×2 / 2-col / 2-row / single by screen; **30px gap** between months.
- Request log table matches app Sent ops: Date, Time, API, Sent From / Type, Header, Feature, Code path, Count. Sticky **Total** row under Count (sum of filtered groups). Row click opens ops popup (Time, From, Action, Received, Failed).
- Log / ops footer pager: rewind « / ‹ / page range / › / forward » arrows (not Earlier/Later text). Same 32px height. Request log pages **groups** (table rows), not Count-column hits. Footer/toolbar: `Group {n} / Log {n}`. Tick boxes + Delete remove selected groups from `pl_usage_request`.
- Request log / Sent ops popups are **draggable** (header) and **resizable** from 4 sides + 4 corners.
